WEBVTT

00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.130
Can you imagine...

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:17.470
...a life in which you could
never touch the one you love?

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.310
He takes the life of whatever he touches.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:23.770
That was the curse the witch put on him.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:28.060
Plants, animals... and people
are no exception, of course.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:31.480
Regarding her son, doomed to live his life
without knowing the warmth of another,

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.150
his mother only complained.

00:00:34.150 --> 00:00:36.660
"That child is like Death incarnate..."

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.660
she said.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:44.370
Don't ask me why, but lately I feel like
all we do is talk about your clothes.

00:00:44.370 --> 00:00:48.130
Alice, I noticed you only wear
black both in and out of uniform.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:49.000
Why is that?

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.710
I like the color black.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.670
I'd like to see you wear some different
colored clothes for a change.

00:00:53.670 --> 00:00:56.630
I kind of like white myself.
It looks so simple and honest.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:58.800
If you say it's all right, Your Grace...

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:00.140
By all means, give it a try.

00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:02.100
I think you'd look great in
a casual white dress...

00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:03.560
...and a formal gown, too...

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.070
Is something the matter?

00:01:10.070 --> 00:01:11.980
It's nothing. Nothing at all...

00:02:42.030 --> 00:02:44.240
"Episode 7: The Duke's and
Alice's Uneventful Day"

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.870
What is that unpleasant-looking thing?

00:02:46.870 --> 00:02:51.580
It's a magic pot. They say that some
witch made it and cared for it daily.

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:53.290
A witch's tool?

00:02:53.290 --> 00:02:56.250
I happened to see it in town
the other day, so I bought it.

00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:59.340
It arrived just now.

00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:01.260
It even comes with a book of recipes.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:02.640
Pretty exciting, don't you think?

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:06.010
I fail to see what you find
so exciting about it...

00:03:06.010 --> 00:03:08.430
Why don't we try cooking with it?

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.730
There's something I'd like
you to sample, Your Grace.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:14.980
Sure, I don't mind, but do you really
need to get this close to tell me?

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:19.320
If this is a witch's tool, then it's
not for normal cooking, right?

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:20.780
What exactly do you want to make?

00:03:20.780 --> 00:03:23.620
A love potion...
I mean, just some soup.

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:25.280
You totally let that slip!

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:28.500
All the ingredients are now ready.

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:30.290
Shall we get started?

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:33.040
Do I really have to
take part in this, too?

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:34.080
Yes, you do.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.960
We're doing this for you, Your Grace.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:38.840
I'm amazed you can say
that with a straight face.

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:41.510
This pot is quite useful.

00:03:41.510 --> 00:03:44.890
I'd really like you to see it
in action, Your Grace.

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.430
"C'mon and be my girl."

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.850
I-I wouldn't be caught dead
with the likes of you!

00:03:53.850 --> 00:03:56.650
This way you don't have to
use a stove to heat it up.

00:03:56.650 --> 00:03:59.230
What sort of taste do
witches have, anyway?

00:03:59.230 --> 00:04:02.530
Well, I guess I got some idea of what it
is from going to that witches' sabbath...

00:04:02.530 --> 00:04:05.780
Once the pot comes to a boil,
we add the ingredients.

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:08.200
Seasoned lizard's tail.

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.950
Amoebas. Red clay soil.

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:12.290
Snail's shell.
Fur from a cat's back--

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:15.000
Hang on there! There's no way
those could be cooking ingredients!

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:17.000
--I'm the one who's going to drink this!
--Sneak a peek!

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:19.300
Let's continue, shall we?

00:04:19.300 --> 00:04:21.920
I'm such an easy target...

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.970
Witches...

00:04:27.970 --> 00:04:29.850
The more I encounter,
the less I understand...

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:31.810
There are witches like
the one that cursed me...

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:35.520
...and others like Cuff and Zain
who are friendly.

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:38.520
I suggest that you give up now.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:41.030
I can't do that...

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:45.530
But, then again, I also don't know
what my next move should be...

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:47.950
What the heck are you
staring at, you freakin' perv?!

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:49.740
I-I'm so sorry!

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:50.740
Your Grace?

00:04:50.740 --> 00:04:53.750
It looks like this magic pot
has other handy features...

00:04:53.750 --> 00:04:55.750
...that we can use by saying
the magic words.

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.170
Um, like what?

00:04:57.170 --> 00:05:01.630
"Say, you're actually pretty cute
when you take off your glasses."

00:05:01.630 --> 00:05:03.010
Wha--?!

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:04.630
You idiot!

00:05:04.630 --> 00:05:07.840
This is a spell that allows you
to make a smokescreen easily.

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:10.640
Like there's ever a time you need to make
a smokescreen when you're cooking!

00:05:15.730 --> 00:05:18.400
And now this is where
you come in, Your Grace.

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:23.690
As you think of all the fun and happy
things in your life, stir the pot.

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:24.990
Um, okay.

00:05:24.990 --> 00:05:29.030
Fun things, happy things...

00:05:29.030 --> 00:05:35.370
Happy things, happy things,
happy things, happy things...

00:05:37.750 --> 00:05:39.960
I got distracted at the end there...

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.340
It's finished.

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:44.130
Actually, this isn't just some soup.

00:05:44.130 --> 00:05:47.260
Uh, you said so yourself
before we started.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:50.050
I was amazed when I saw this in town.

00:05:50.050 --> 00:05:53.810
See? It's a potion to
remove a witch's curse.

00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:56.020
So, it wasn't a love potion?

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:58.900
They say if you get distracted while
you're stirring, it won't be as effective.

00:05:58.900 --> 00:06:01.020
I thought I'd warn you at first, but...

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.150
No, I'd just get more distracted that way!

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:05.780
In fact, I <i>did </i>get distracted a bit!

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:07.320
It says it's all right...

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:10.950
...as long as you don't think about
the curse while you're stirring.

00:06:10.950 --> 00:06:15.500
So, this magic pot and those
ingredients were all for me?

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:16.450
Yes.

00:06:16.450 --> 00:06:19.960
Since the witch that cursed
you is no longer living,

00:06:19.960 --> 00:06:23.250
I thought we should try anything we can.

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.760
It may be a bit hot, but...

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.010
Okay.

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:28.170
I'll try it.

00:06:30.840 --> 00:06:33.390
This tastes like hell...

00:06:33.390 --> 00:06:34.930
Your Grace, let's test it out.

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.280
It didn't work...

00:06:45.280 --> 00:06:46.530
We'll just have to accept it, I guess.

00:06:46.530 --> 00:06:50.910
According to that witch Daleth,
it's not your run-of-the-mill curse.

00:06:50.910 --> 00:06:55.080
More importantly, I was happy for
your feelings of encouragement.

00:06:55.080 --> 00:06:56.450
Thanks.

00:06:56.450 --> 00:07:00.750
I'll look for some other way
to break the curse, then.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:02.750
Okay, I'm counting on you.

00:07:02.750 --> 00:07:04.090
So...

00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.750
What should we do with this?

00:07:05.750 --> 00:07:08.420
If we tried to get rid of it,
it might curse us...

00:07:09.920 --> 00:07:11.680
You're giving this to me?

00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:14.350
Um, yeah. It's a magic pot.

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:16.350
I'll let you decide what to do with it.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:20.190
Oh, what a sharp dresser!

00:07:20.190 --> 00:07:22.560
You mean, I'm going to be <i>his</i>?

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.110
A talking pot?

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:25.650
Fascinating.

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.320
Thank you for this.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.150
Oh, my! We're going on
our honeymoon already?

00:07:30.150 --> 00:07:33.320
Though I am but a humble pot, I hope
we'll be together for better or worse.

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.040
V-Viola?!

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.120
How long have you been there?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.830
Viola, wait a sec!

00:07:39.830 --> 00:07:42.120
Rob! Hide that pot!

00:07:42.120 --> 00:07:44.290
Alice! Stop Viola!

00:07:44.290 --> 00:07:45.290
Alice!

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:13.700
Wow, this sheet music's so hard to read...

00:08:13.700 --> 00:08:15.780
What is this, anyway?

00:08:15.780 --> 00:08:18.830
It's the final score that the composer
McFarlane wrote before he died.

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.910
They say it's the world's most
beautiful piece of music.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.790
McFarlane?

00:08:23.790 --> 00:08:26.710
But it's got quite a checkered history...

00:08:26.710 --> 00:08:29.210
They say that anyone who
performs it goes mad.

00:08:29.210 --> 00:08:30.550
What the--?! That's scary!

00:08:30.550 --> 00:08:32.920
But they also say that if
you can play it perfectly,

00:08:32.920 --> 00:08:35.390
you'll be cleansed of your curse.

00:08:35.390 --> 00:08:36.340
Cleansed, huh?

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.560
I hope that things will
work out this time...

00:08:38.560 --> 00:08:40.270
So, how about it? Will you give it a try?

00:08:40.270 --> 00:08:43.690
I-I'll do it, so stop using your
breasts to pressure me into it!

00:08:51.480 --> 00:08:55.860
While the music may be hard to read,
it's certainly a lovely tune.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:56.870
But...

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:01.870
...who the heck is this guy?

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:03.960
You can see me, can't you?

00:09:03.960 --> 00:09:06.330
Woah, he spoke to me.

00:09:06.330 --> 00:09:09.000
Are you McFarlane?

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:10.300
Indeed, I am.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:12.840
No one will play this perfectly, so...

00:09:12.840 --> 00:09:16.010
...I have become a ghost to watch
over it even in death.

00:09:16.010 --> 00:09:17.010
Think you can do it?

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:20.060
If you stick your head in my face
like that, I'll mess up!

00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.220
Aw, jeez.

00:09:21.220 --> 00:09:24.640
I, like, totally shouldn't have put the
music on black paper so it'd look cool.

00:09:24.640 --> 00:09:26.940
Like, even I totally
have trouble reading it.

00:09:26.940 --> 00:09:29.560
You did it just so it'd look cool?

00:09:29.560 --> 00:09:32.230
Your Grace, are you all right?

00:09:32.230 --> 00:09:34.780
Don't tell me you've actually gone mad.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:35.700
No, of course I haven't!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.280
It's no use trying to explain it to her.

00:09:37.280 --> 00:09:40.370
You, the performer,
are the only one who can see me.

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.870
By the way, this chick is far out.

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:45.040
What? Are you kids going steady?

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:47.710
People back then used
words that are so passé...

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.540
Hehe, watch this.

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:52.710
While I may be a ghost,
I can do stuff like this, too.

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:53.590
Whoosh!

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:56.300
My, what a naughty gust of wind!

00:09:56.300 --> 00:09:57.800
Did you see that, Your Grace?

00:09:57.800 --> 00:09:59.840
No, I didn't! I didn't see anything!

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:02.310
What do you think you're doing, McFarlane?

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.850
Like, I haven't messed around
with a girl in, like, centuries!

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:07.890
Aren't I allowed to,
like, have a little fun?

00:10:07.890 --> 00:10:10.230
Just concentrate on your performance!

00:10:10.230 --> 00:10:11.730
Then, let me!

00:10:13.940 --> 00:10:18.780
Oh yeah, now I'm gonna slip this
strange strap off her shoulder like so!

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:21.320
Oh, that naughty wind is at it again...

00:10:21.320 --> 00:10:22.830
Are you watching, Your Grace?

00:10:22.830 --> 00:10:24.580
It's okay, I'm not watching.

00:10:24.580 --> 00:10:25.830
Why aren't you watching?

00:10:25.830 --> 00:10:26.750
Why should I?

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:30.330
Oh, no! What's to become of me?
That naughty wind is...

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:32.340
How many times is that naughty
wind going to blow, anyway?

00:10:32.340 --> 00:10:34.210
Besides, it's you that's
doing the stripping!

00:10:34.210 --> 00:10:35.760
I can't take it anymore!

00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:38.930
Hey baby, pucker up and gimme a kiss!

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:41.180
No, anything but that!

00:10:41.180 --> 00:10:42.470
Please, knock it off.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:52.310
Her eyes looked so cold
when she rejected me!

00:10:52.310 --> 00:10:54.730
Quit making me dodge you
while I'm playing!

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:57.610
You wouldn't happen to be one of
those people who can see ghosts?

00:10:57.610 --> 00:10:59.490
No, I'm not.

00:10:59.490 --> 00:11:01.030
But you're talking to him!

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:03.320
This leaves me but one objective.

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.120
You must play this song
perfectly to the end...

00:11:06.120 --> 00:11:09.160
--...or else I'll haunt you
for the rest of your life!
--Don't be absurd!

00:11:17.880 --> 00:11:21.720
I must concentrate.
Concentrate on playing...

00:11:21.720 --> 00:11:23.800
The piano is all I've got.

00:11:23.800 --> 00:11:25.640
Always has been, always will be.

00:11:25.640 --> 00:11:27.180
All I can do is play it.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:36.070
For my sake...

00:11:36.070 --> 00:11:39.690
And for the sake of Alice's
and my future together!

00:11:50.870 --> 00:11:54.460
How do you like that, McFarlane?
I played your song perfectly!

00:11:54.460 --> 00:11:56.630
Now I'll be cleansed of my curse.

00:11:57.840 --> 00:11:59.710
Whoa...

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.840
What a splendid performance!

00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:08.680
Thank you, my friend.

00:12:12.140 --> 00:12:14.810
So, <i>you </i>were the curse I'm cleansed of?!

00:12:21.150 --> 00:12:22.530
Good morning, Alice.

00:12:22.530 --> 00:12:24.660
I woke up early, so I came to get you.

00:12:24.660 --> 00:12:26.530
Come to the mansion right away.

00:12:27.700 --> 00:12:30.330
Certainly.
I'm on my way to the door.

00:12:30.330 --> 00:12:32.540
Oh, you've got some clothes on, right?

00:12:32.540 --> 00:12:35.080
I ask because you never wear
anything while you're in your room...

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.330
Don't worry.

00:12:36.330 --> 00:12:38.840
Good morning, Your Grace.

00:12:38.840 --> 00:12:40.670
Lingerie does not count as clothes!

00:12:40.670 --> 00:12:42.380
I put them on by mistake.

00:12:42.380 --> 00:12:44.760
You totally did that on purpose!

00:12:44.760 --> 00:12:49.220
Alice isn't startled at all when
someone sees her bare skin.

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:52.680
I wonder if she even sees me as a guy?

00:12:52.680 --> 00:12:55.520
Come to think of it,
the other day, Viola...

00:12:55.520 --> 00:12:57.860
Yoo-hoo! Dearest Brother!

00:12:57.860 --> 00:13:00.280
You startled me!
Oh, Viola, it's you...

00:13:00.280 --> 00:13:03.900
Oh, quit getting startled at every little
thing. It's so annoying.

00:13:03.900 --> 00:13:06.870
Now, don't get your heart pounding
and fall for me or anything.

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:09.830
What are you going on about with
such a sincere look in your eyes?

00:13:09.830 --> 00:13:11.870
You know about the suspension
bridge effect, right?

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.660
When they're with someone,
people mistake the fear and anxiety...

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:17.500
...making their hearts pound
as love for the other person!

00:13:17.500 --> 00:13:20.300
In other words, all I have to do
is get Alice's heart pounding

00:13:20.300 --> 00:13:22.550
by startling and scaring her.

00:13:22.550 --> 00:13:24.630
This may be worth giving a try.

00:13:25.630 --> 00:13:27.550
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:28.600
Huh?

00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:29.800
Your Grace?

00:13:33.850 --> 00:13:36.020
Ta-da! I was in your blind spot!

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:38.270
--Oh, my!
--Were you startled?

00:13:38.270 --> 00:13:40.230
Yes, I was.

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:42.280
This is going to be tough.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:49.200
A-And now we're getting
to the really scary part...

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:53.080
Th-The man turned his head
and shouted, "I saw that."

00:13:53.080 --> 00:13:55.540
But he had no eyes or nose,

00:13:55.540 --> 00:13:57.830
just a mouth that was
slit from ear to ear.

00:13:57.830 --> 00:13:59.420
Ooh, how scary is that?

00:13:59.420 --> 00:14:01.630
It gives me the chills
just talking about it.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:02.880
That was scary.

00:14:02.880 --> 00:14:05.220
But when the narrator's scared...

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:07.300
...it loses half of its fear factor.

00:14:07.300 --> 00:14:08.760
Oh, really...

00:14:08.760 --> 00:14:10.800
I'm just no good at this.

00:14:10.800 --> 00:14:13.520
McFarlane didn't scare me at all, but...

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:17.020
So, I give your story a score of 98.

00:14:17.020 --> 00:14:19.520
You've got to love her for being
a super lenient grader.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:23.150
Oh, I finally found it!

00:14:23.150 --> 00:14:24.110
What a scary painting!

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:25.150
Is that the right one?

00:14:25.150 --> 00:14:27.990
Huh?! Oh, not this one.

00:14:27.990 --> 00:14:29.410
That's strange.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:33.490
I could've sworn I had a painting of
a woman shedding tears of blood...

00:14:36.370 --> 00:14:37.580
Is...

00:14:37.580 --> 00:14:39.040
...this it?

00:14:40.830 --> 00:14:42.130
Yeah, that's the one.

00:14:42.130 --> 00:14:43.800
What's it doing hanging there?

00:14:43.800 --> 00:14:47.050
The other day, I took it down and put
it in the rack because it's so creepy.

00:14:47.050 --> 00:14:48.430
How strange.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:49.380
That's all you've got to say?!

00:14:49.380 --> 00:14:50.220
Aren't you scared?!

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.550
All right, I'm scared.

00:14:51.550 --> 00:14:52.600
What's with the "all right"?!

00:14:52.600 --> 00:14:56.470
Here I am totally scared, and you mean
to tell me your heart isn't pounding?!

00:14:56.470 --> 00:14:58.060
But my heart <i>is </i>pounding.

00:14:58.060 --> 00:15:01.520
Why don't you put your ear against
my chest and listen for yourself?

00:15:01.520 --> 00:15:02.900
Like I can do that!

00:15:02.900 --> 00:15:04.900
Come on, just think about it.

00:15:04.900 --> 00:15:08.400
The painting moved by itself!
Isn't that scary?

00:15:08.400 --> 00:15:09.320
It certainly is.

00:15:09.320 --> 00:15:12.780
Aw, come on! Why won't you get scared?

00:15:12.780 --> 00:15:16.790
If your heart doesn't start pounding, you
won't feel the suspension bridge effect!

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.750
My heart really <i>is </i>pounding.

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.750
Because I'm with <i>you</i>, Your Grace.

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:24.130
She looks even cuter than usual.

00:15:24.130 --> 00:15:26.250
This may be the suspension
bridge effect at work.

00:15:27.630 --> 00:15:29.220
But...

00:15:29.220 --> 00:15:32.010
...how did this painting get here?

00:15:32.010 --> 00:15:34.550
Alice, didn't you hang that
painting there yesterday

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:37.100
because there was some
extra space there?

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:39.230
Shh! It's our secret.

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:44.060
The more I look at it...

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:46.150
...the scarier it gets!

00:15:46.150 --> 00:15:47.150
Oh! Your Grace!

00:15:47.150 --> 00:15:48.740
Look out behind you!

00:15:50.530 --> 00:15:51.530
Oh...

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:54.620
--Darn it!
--No, don't touch it!

00:15:54.620 --> 00:15:57.040
That plant has been here from when this
mansion was the family's main residence.

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:59.200
It only flowers once every 50 years.

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:01.040
It's extremely valuable.

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:05.210
I'm so sorry!

00:16:09.880 --> 00:16:13.430
What are you doing in there, Your Grace?

00:16:15.760 --> 00:16:18.520
What you did back there
was only an accident.

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:22.190
Still, I'd prefer not to face Rob
until he calms down.

00:16:22.190 --> 00:16:23.690
Anyway, shut the door.

00:16:23.690 --> 00:16:25.150
I don't want to be found just yet.

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:26.820
Very well.

00:16:26.820 --> 00:16:28.440
Why'd you come in here?!

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:30.940
Well, you asked me to shut the door...

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.530
What is Rob like when he gets angry?

00:16:33.530 --> 00:16:34.780
He's pretty scary.

00:16:34.780 --> 00:16:36.200
He doesn't chew you out or anything,

00:16:36.200 --> 00:16:39.330
but he won't forgive you until
you've reflected on your actions.

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.250
I'd kind of like to see that.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.370
You on the receiving end of
his anger, that is, Your Grace.

00:16:44.370 --> 00:16:46.920
--Huh?!
--Your Grace?

00:16:46.920 --> 00:16:48.500
Are you in here?

00:16:48.500 --> 00:16:49.590
It's Rob.

00:16:49.590 --> 00:16:51.260
I'll protect you.

00:16:56.470 --> 00:16:59.680
Whew! I was really freaked out
for a minute there.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:02.850
You know, it's not safe for you
to get that close to me.

00:17:02.850 --> 00:17:04.440
I'm sorry, I wasn't thinking...

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:06.560
So, where will you hide next?

00:17:06.560 --> 00:17:08.230
This is starting to get fun!

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:09.730
This is a huge mansion.

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:12.030
There are lots of places to hide.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:16.410
But Rob knows this place inside out.
Where can I hide and not be found?

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:17.740
How about under here?

00:17:17.740 --> 00:17:20.370
Oh, yeah, what a great choice.
It's so romantic...

00:17:20.370 --> 00:17:21.830
Quit fooling around, would you?!

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:24.040
I've been looking for you, Your Grace.

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.340
I wanted to speak with you
about the flowerpot.

00:17:28.340 --> 00:17:29.920
Uh, um...

00:17:31.170 --> 00:17:33.130
I-I'm Alice.

00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:35.800
I pride myself on being able to wake up
after exactly seven hours of sleep.

00:17:35.800 --> 00:17:37.590
Oh, it's you, Alice.

00:17:37.590 --> 00:17:39.680
Pardon me.

00:17:39.680 --> 00:17:42.770
How senile can you get?

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.770
That was a pretty good impression of me.

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.520
Th-Thanks...

00:17:48.730 --> 00:17:50.020
So...

00:17:50.020 --> 00:17:53.280
...we wound up hiding underneath my bed.

00:17:53.280 --> 00:17:56.780
This is a surprisingly good hiding place,
if somewhat ordinary.

00:17:58.070 --> 00:18:01.280
I wanted to be in a dark,
cramped space with you, Your Grace.

00:18:01.280 --> 00:18:04.830
Oh, so for you, hiding from Rob
isn't the objective anymore, huh?

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:06.620
Did you know, Your Grace?

00:18:06.620 --> 00:18:10.340
Hide-and-seek was originally
a game for adults.

00:18:10.340 --> 00:18:11.750
You've gotta be kidding...

00:18:11.750 --> 00:18:13.130
Wait, really?

00:18:13.130 --> 00:18:17.340
Are you looking forward to
becoming an adult, Your Grace?

00:18:17.340 --> 00:18:19.640
Um, more or less.

00:18:19.640 --> 00:18:21.810
I want to get to know
the pleasures of alcohol.

00:18:21.810 --> 00:18:25.560
It'd be wonderful to have dinner and
drinks with someone like you every night.

00:18:26.890 --> 00:18:28.900
My heart's really pounding now.

00:18:28.900 --> 00:18:32.110
Could this be the suspension
bridge effect at work?

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:42.870
I'm sorry to interrupt you, but...

00:18:42.870 --> 00:18:44.120
Rob?!

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:46.710
What's all this?

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:50.130
I found them among the shards of the
flowerpot you broke, Your Grace.

00:18:50.130 --> 00:18:54.170
I believe they had been stolen from the
lady and senior lady of the house.

00:18:54.170 --> 00:18:56.260
From Mother and Grandmother?

00:18:56.260 --> 00:18:59.260
Back when this mansion was still
the family's main residence,

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.800
we had an incident involving a servant
who stole some of the family's valuables.

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:06.470
The thief must have hidden the stolen
items inside the flowerpot temporarily,

00:19:06.470 --> 00:19:08.940
and was never able to retrieve them.

00:19:08.940 --> 00:19:11.480
Anyhow, I'm so glad you found them.

00:19:11.480 --> 00:19:14.020
I'm sure the lady of the house
will be very pleased.

00:19:14.020 --> 00:19:16.570
You were great, Your Grace.
Just like a master detective.

00:19:16.570 --> 00:19:17.900
Well...

00:19:17.900 --> 00:19:20.110
I didn't really
do anything, though...

00:19:20.110 --> 00:19:22.620
Oh, and I'm going to have a nice,
long chat with you later on...

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:25.700
...regarding the flowerpot you broke.

00:19:25.700 --> 00:19:28.000
Guess I'm going to get
a talking-to after all...

00:21:04.550 --> 00:21:06.050
Where am I?

00:21:07.220 --> 00:21:09.140
Are you awake, Your Grace?

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:10.930
Alice!

00:21:10.930 --> 00:21:12.930
Where the heck are we?

00:21:12.930 --> 00:21:14.390
This is a dream.

00:21:14.390 --> 00:21:15.520
A dream?

00:21:15.520 --> 00:21:18.150
Don't you remember?

00:21:18.150 --> 00:21:21.230
A moment ago, we were looking
through old books in the library,

00:21:21.230 --> 00:21:24.320
trying to find some way
to break your curse.

00:21:24.320 --> 00:21:26.360
And the second we opened
one of the books...

00:21:28.240 --> 00:21:31.040
Bring me the white rabbit
that carries a pocket watch.

00:21:31.040 --> 00:21:33.540
As a token of my appreciation,
I shall grant you a wish.

00:21:33.540 --> 00:21:37.460
After that, I lost consciousness,
and the next thing I knew, I was here.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:42.210
Our real selves are probably
asleep in the library.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:43.380
I see.

00:21:43.380 --> 00:21:46.930
So, if we catch that white rabbit
and give it to the girl, then...

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:51.260
Yes. This time we may finally be able
to break your curse, Your Grace.

00:21:51.260 --> 00:21:53.350
--Plus...
--Alice?!

00:21:53.350 --> 00:21:56.140
This is a dream, so it's all right.

00:21:56.140 --> 00:21:57.560
See?

00:21:57.560 --> 00:21:58.690
Oh, you're right.

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:00.570
I can't feel a thing.

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:04.740
Why'd you put my hand to your breast
when I can't enjoy how it feels?

00:22:04.740 --> 00:22:08.450
I couldn't feel anything! Anything at all!

00:22:08.450 --> 00:22:09.870
Hey, a rabbit just...

00:22:09.870 --> 00:22:10.870
Huh?

00:22:13.080 --> 00:22:14.700
Let's go after it, Your Grace.

00:22:14.700 --> 00:22:15.960
Um, okay...

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:47.150
We were having so much fun
that we got totally carried away.

00:22:47.150 --> 00:22:49.030
That's one of our bad habits.

00:22:49.030 --> 00:22:51.660
It'll be seven hours
since we arrived here.

00:22:51.660 --> 00:22:54.200
We should be waking up soon.

00:22:54.200 --> 00:22:56.620
Oh, right. Exactly seven hours of sleep...

00:22:57.540 --> 00:23:01.170
Since we've got this rare opportunity,
shall we end it with a kiss?

00:23:01.170 --> 00:23:05.760
Huh?! Well yeah, this is a dream
and all, so we could, but...

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:07.970
Kiss me, please.

00:23:07.970 --> 00:23:09.180
Alice...

00:23:13.640 --> 00:23:15.100
This time...

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:17.600
...I won't back out.

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:22.520
Jeez, you guys are totally useless!

00:23:22.520 --> 00:23:25.900
You go all lovey-dovey on me and can't
even be bothered to look for the rabbit!

00:23:27.280 --> 00:23:29.360
Don't you ever summon me again, egghead!

00:23:29.360 --> 00:23:30.990
And drop dead while you're at it!

00:23:34.870 --> 00:23:38.620
I wonder if I can pick the
dream up where I left off...

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:46.210
"White Snow, Black Clothes."
